It replaces the character that spans the cut with a space in both segments. This seems wrong if the character is a multi-cell character.

If `cell_pos > cut`, it means the character at `text[pos-1]` (since `pos` was incremented) spans the cut.
`before` is `text[:pos]`. `before[:pos-1]` is `text[:pos-1]`.
So it's replacing the character at `pos-1` with a space.

